#TODO: Update the unit test with new Scenario
Feature: Read Policy

  Background:
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ",
         "description": "FAQ",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag1",
            "tag2"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-R1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: Get Policies
    Given The Resource Admin wants to get All Policy with API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get all Policy
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And a list of all Policy is returned in the response
      """json
      {
         "results": [
            {
               "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
               "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
               "resourceType": "FAQ",
               "scope": "",
               "actions": [
                  "view",
                  "update",
                  "create",
                  "delete"
               ],
               "roles": [
                  "ADMIN-R1"
               ],
               "effect": "ALLOW"
            }
         ],
         "metadata": {
            "totalCount": 1,
            "totalPageCount": 1,
            "size": 10
         }
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: Get a Policy by key
    Given Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Policy with the key 'FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Policy by key
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And return the Policy
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-R1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """

  Scenario: Positive: Get a Policy with an existing/duplicate key but with different project
    Given a Resource Type for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ",
         "name": "FAQ",
         "description": "Frequently Asked Question Project 2",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "tags": [
            "tag1",
            "tag2"
         ]
      }
      """
    And a Policy for API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722' with specific attributes exists
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-R1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """
    And Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Policy with the key 'FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY' and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57722'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Policy by key
    Then the request is successfully with response code 200
    And return the Policy
      """json
      {
         "key": "FAQ_ADMIN_POLICY",
         "description": "FAQ resource policy for Admin",
         "resourceType": "FAQ",
         "scope": "",
         "actions": [
            "view",
            "update",
            "create",
            "delete"
         ],
         "roles": [
            "ADMIN-R1"
         ],
         "effect": "ALLOW"
      }
      """

  Scenario: Negative: Get a Policy by a non-existent Key
    Given Resource Admin wants to retrieve a Policy with the key "wrong_key" and API key '22ee17bd-699e-4b6b-a30b-e854e6c57552'
    When the Resource Admin requests to get Policy by key
    Then the request is fails with response code 404
    And the response body read includes status 404 and error message 'Not Found'
